Messaging: SDD

Purpose:
  Messaging technology catalog with comparison criteria, selection rules,
  and integration patterns. Root stack/ defines reusable messaging knowledge;
  instances/vkard.az/stack/ stores the selected messaging for the project.

Catalog:
  RabbitMQ:
    Type: Message Broker
    Pros:
      - Mature and stable
      - Flexible routing
      - Management UI
      - Multi-protocol (AMQP, MQTT)
    Cons:
      - Lower throughput than Kafka
      - Cluster complexity
    BestFor:
      - Task queues
      - Microservice communication
      - Reliable delivery
    AvoidWhen:
      - High-throughput event streaming
    Patterns:
      - Work queues
      - Publish/Subscribe
      - Routing
      - RPC

  Kafka:
    Type: Event Streaming
    Pros:
      - High throughput
      - Distributed
      - Persistent log
      - Stream processing
    Cons:
      - Complex operations
      - Higher resource usage
    BestFor:
      - Event sourcing
      - Log aggregation
      - Real-time streaming
    AvoidWhen:
      - Simple task queues
      - Low throughput

  NATS:
    Type: Message Broker
    Pros:
      - High performance
      - Simple deployment
      - JetStream for persistence
      - Low latency
    Cons:
      - Smaller ecosystem
      - Less enterprise adoption
    BestFor:
      - Microservice communication
      - Real-time systems
      - Cloud-native
    AvoidWhen:
      - Complex routing needs

  AWS SQS/SNS:
    Type: Managed Cloud
    Pros:
      - Fully managed
      - No infrastructure
      - AWS integration
    Cons:
      - Vendor lock-in
      - Cost at scale
    BestFor:
      - AWS-native architectures
      - Serverless
    AvoidWhen:
      - Multi-cloud

SelectionRules:
  - Throughput: message volume requirements
  - Latency: delivery latency requirements
  - Durability: persistence requirements
  - Ordering: message ordering guarantees
  - Complexity: operational overhead tolerance
  - Integration: compatibility with existing stack

TechnologyScore:
  Throughput: 0-25
  Latency: 0-20
  Durability: 0-15
  Ordering: 0-10
  Complexity: 0-10
  Integration: 0-20

State: +
  